 ## Overview
-Perpendicular Slice Extraction Geometry computes the geometric properties of a slice perpendicular to a specified anatomical axis (x, y, or z) at a specific RAS index. It returns the slice dimensions, a plane matrix defining orientation and position in RAS space, and a `sliceAccess` function to map 2D slice coordinates to 3D volume data indices. It differs from [Plane Slicing](845-plane-slicing.md) by enforcing strict alignment with the primary axes and handling the coordinate transformation between RAS (Right-Anterior-Superior) and IJK (voxel) spaces explicitly through rotation and offset calculations.
+Perpendicular Slice Extraction Geometry computes the geometric properties of a slice perpendicular to a specified anatomical axis (x, y, or z) at a specific RAS index [S1, unofficial]. It returns the slice dimensions, a plane matrix defining orientation and position in RAS space, and a `sliceAccess` function to map 2D slice coordinates to 3D volume data indices [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Plane Slicing](845-plane-slicing.md) by enforcing strict alignment with the primary axes and handling the coordinate transformation between RAS (Right-Anterior-Superior) and IJK (voxel) spaces explicitly through rotation and offset calculations [G].
 
